findings.cause:
D2, the WVU silver trims too much (382 silver).
the Studio regex (course-description v1) ends a "PR:" sentence at a full stop followed by a capital letter. When the description opens with "(" the match runs on to a later full stop, so real sentences are dropped:
- [CPE 450](http://catalog.wvu.edu/westvirginiauniversityinstituteoftechnology/courses/):
  - source: "PR: EE 251. (VLSI-Very Large Scale Integrated) circuit design, … CAD tools are used for projects. (3 hr. lec.).";
  - silver: "CAD tools are used for projects. (3 hr. lec.).";
  - extracted: everything after "PR: EE 251.".
- [ADV 419](http://catalog.wvu.edu/undergraduate/collegeofcreativeartsandmedia/):
  - silver: "Students learn how to use advertising…";
  - extracted: "(Advertising minors only.) Introduces students to the concept of branding. Students learn…".

D6, the UALR silver is cut at a line break (5 silver). For [ECED 44003](https://catalog.ualr.edu/preview_course_nopop.php?catoid=43&coid=137633):
- the silver value ends "…an endorsement in Pre-K (Ages 3-";
- the extracted value carries on through "4). Restrictions will be…".

findings.fix:
UARK needs a narrower description reader. Read the narrative paragraphs and leave out:
- headings and taglines;
- Approved Provider # lines;
- lists after a lead-in such as "Objectives" or "students will:";
- closing calls to action and boilerplate.
